# GRCh38 silencer training and evaluation datasets

This directory contains two independent organizations produced from the same
native-distribution selection:

1. a fixed chr1/chr2 train-validation-test benchmark for learning curves; and
2. four chromosome-fold outer datasets with a common fold5 test set.

For each chromosome, the usable paired count is the smaller of the available
positive and negative pools. This retains all 202,423 generated negatives and
selects the same number of positives, removing only the 70 positives for which
`genNullSeqs()` did not find a match. No EVN chromosome quotas are imposed.

All positive and negative BED/FASTA pairs remain synchronized by record
position. The selection seed is 42. Negative membership follows its
chromosome-specific source pool; the synthetic null BED coordinate may occur on
another chromosome.

## Fixed learning-curve benchmark

This routing is unchanged by the five-fold outer redesign.

| split | chromosome membership | positive records | negative records | purpose |
|:------|:----------------------|-----------------:|-----------------:|:--------|
| Training 100% | Paired chr3-chr22 and chrX records | 158,088 | 158,088 | Learning-curve model fitting |
| Validation | Paired chr1 records | 29,759 | 29,759 | Early stopping/model selection |
| Test | Paired chr2 records | 14,576 | 14,576 | Final evaluation only |
| **Complete benchmark** | chr1-chr22 and chrX | **202,423** | **202,423** | — |

The fixed files are:

```text
train_100_pos.bed
train_100_pos.fa
train_100_neg.bed
train_100_neg.fa
validation_pos.bed
validation_pos.fa
validation_neg.bed
validation_neg.fa
test_pos.bed
test_pos.fa
test_neg.bed
test_neg.fa
train_100_manifest.tsv
train_100_summary.json
```

Validation and test are written once and are not percentage-subsetted. The
nested subsets in `../learning_curves/` remain prefixes of the 158,088-record
training pool:

| training percentage | records per class |
|--------------------:|------------------:|
| 10%  | 15,808 |
| 20%  | 31,617 |
| 40%  | 63,235 |
| 60%  | 94,852 |
| 80%  | 126,470 |
| 100% | 158,088 |

## Five-fold outer experiments

The outer analysis uses the five chromosome folds documented in `../folds/`.
Folds 1-4 are development folds and fold5 is the common final test set. Outer N
omits development fold N, then uses the other three development folds for
training and validation.

Validation chromosomes were selected from an included development fold to be
close to 10% of the pre-validation development pool. Counts are per class.

| outer set | training folds before validation removal | omitted fold | validation chromosome | validation fraction | training records | validation records | final test |
|:----------|:-----------------------------------------|:------------:|:----------------------|--------------------:|-----------------:|-------------------:|:-----------|
| Outer 1 | 2 + 3 + 4 | 1 | chr4 | 9.14% | 110,021 | 11,065 | fold5 (40,598) |
| Outer 2 | 1 + 3 + 4 | 2 | chr11 | 10.32% | 109,072 | 12,558 | fold5 (40,598) |
| Outer 3 | 1 + 2 + 4 | 3 | chr11 | 10.34% | 108,838 | 12,558 | fold5 (40,598) |
| Outer 4 | 1 + 2 + 3 | 4 | chr11 | 10.35% | 108,805 | 12,558 | fold5 (40,598) |

Each `outerN/` directory contains separate
`train_{pos,neg}.{bed,fa}` and `validation_{pos,neg}.{bed,fa}` files. Test data
is not copied into each outer directory; all four models use
`../folds/fold5/{fold5,neg1x_fold5}.{bed,fa}`. Fold5 must never control early
stopping, checkpoint selection, hyperparameter selection, or thresholds.
